    "ls|LS17_S2_U_138": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF DEFENCE \nDEPARTMENT OF DEFENCE \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 138 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 27th November, 2019 \n \nCYBER WARFARE THREATS \n \n*138. DR. (PROF.) KIRIT PREMJIBHAI SOLANKI: \nWill the Minister of DEFENCE j{kk ea=h  \nbe pleased to state: \n  \n(a) whether the Indian Armed forces are prepared for handling cyber warfare threats; \n(b) if so, the details thereof; and \n(c) whether the Government has taken  steps and allocated funds to enhance the  \ncapability for undertaking offensive cyber warfare attacks? \n \n \n \nA    N    S    W    E    R \n \nMINISTER OF DEFENCE                                    (SHRI RAJNATH SINGH) \n      j{kk ea=h                  ¼Jh jktukFk flag ) \n \n \n \n(a) to (c):  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n******* \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (c) OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO. 138 FOR ANSWER ON 27.11.2019 \nREGARDING ‘CYBER WARFARE THREATS’ \n \n(a) to  (c):  Yes, Sir.  Government has approved establishment of Defence Cyber \nAgency to control and coordinate the Joint Cyber operations.  To mitigate cyber \nthreats, all the three Services have established their respective Cyber Emergency \nResponse Teams (CERT).  Ade quate safeguards have been instituted in the form of \nCyber Audits, Physical Checks and Policy Guidelines to ensure a robust cyber posture \nof armed forces.  Sufficient budgetary allocation is being provided for Cyber \noperations and capability development. \n  \n  \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S2_U_139": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 139 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18.11.2019 \n \nNEEM \n \n139. SHRI FEROZE VARUN GANDHI:   \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n(a) the State-wise distribution of registrants under the National Employability Enhancement \nMission(NEEM) Scheme; \n(b) the State-wise distribution of NEEM facilitators/NEEM Agents under the NEEM Scheme; \nand \n(c) number of registrants/trainee su nder the NEEM scheme whose employment have been \nregularized/recruited into organizations after the completion of their training under the \nNEEM Scheme? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n \n(SHRI RAMESH POKHRIYAL ‘NISHANK’) \n(a) & (b) : The state -wise distribution of registrants and facilitators under the National \nEmployability Enhancement Mission (NEEM) Scheme is at annexure I and II respectively.  \n \n(c): NEEM Scheme is not an employment guarantee scheme. As per the data available with \nAICTE, 21 NEEM f acilitators and 2574 no. of trainees have been regularized/ placed in their \ntrainee company after the completion of their training under the NEEM Scheme. \n \n \n \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nANNEXURE AS REFERRED TO IN PART (a)  & (b)  OF THE LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 139  TO BE ANSWERED ON 18.11.2019 ASKED BY SHRI FEROZE VARUN \nGANDHI REGARDING NEEM \n \nS.No. State Total Enrolled Trainees  \n1 Andhra Pradesh  1675 \n2 Delhi 19 \n3 Himachal Pradesh 658 \n4 Karnataka 146080 \n5 Madhya Pradesh 5981 \n6 Maharashtra 225451 \n7 Odisha 4494 \n8 Tamil Nadu 13194 \n9 Telangana 14 \n10 Uttar Pradesh 5420 \n11 Uttrakhand 673 \n12 West Bengal 1078 \n  Total   404737 \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nANNEXURE AS REFERRED TO IN PART (a) & (b) OF THE LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO. 139 TO BE ANSWERED ON 18.11.2019 ASKED BY SHRI FEROZE VARUN \nGANDHI REGARDING NEEM \