ndation Uttar Pradesh \n42 Aditya Charitable Trust Uttarakhand \n43 Orion Educational Society West Bengal \n \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S2_U_14": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF SCHOOL EDUCATION & LITERACY \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nSTARRED QUESTION NO.14 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 18.11.2019 \n \nNEW KENDRIYA VIDYALAYAS \n \n*14. MS. DIYA KUMARI:  \nWill the Minister of HUMAN RESO URCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased \nto state: \n(a)  the total number of Kendriya Vidyalayas (KVs) that have st udents \nenrolled in the country and abroad;  \n(b)  the teacher-student rat io in such Vidyalayas;  \n(c)  the number of new KVs that a re being opened in the country  and \nabroad;  \n(d)  whether the Government is planning to set up new KVs in Ra jasthan \nand if so, the details thereof; and  \n(e)  whether any of the said K Vs will be set up in Rajsamand an d if so, the \ndetails thereof and if not, the reasons therefor? \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI RAMESH POKHRIYAL ‘NISHANK’) \n \n(a) to (e) A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n****** \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY  TO PARTS (a) TO (e) OF THE \nLOK SABHA STARRED Q U E S T I O N  N O .  1 4  R A I S E D  B Y  M S .  D I Y A  \nKUMARI, HON’BLE MEMBER OF PA RLIAMENT TO BE ANSWERED ON \n18TH NOVEMBER, 2019 REGARDING NEW KENDRIYA VIDYALAYAS.  \n \n(a) The total number of Kendriya  Vidyalayas (KVs) that have stu dents \nenrolled in the country and abroad are 1227. \n(b) The teacher student r atio in KVs is 1:27. \n(c)  Opening of KVs is a continuo us process. Proposals for open ing of new \nKVs are considered only if spons ored by Ministries or Departmen ts of the \nGovernment of India/State Governments / Union Territories Admin istrations \nthereby committing resources for setting up a new KV as well as  the \navailability of necessary sanction of the Government.  The prop osals received \nfrom various sponsoring authorit ies for opening of new KVs also  h a v e  t o  \ncompete among other proposals under the “Challenge Method”. \n(d) 76 KVs are already functioning  in the State of Rajasthan. D etails are \nannexed. In addition a new KV ha d been sanctioned in March, 201 9 at \nPratapgarh. The State Government  o f  R a j a s t h a n ,  b e i n g  t h e  s p o n s oring \nauthority is required to transfer the requisite extent of land in favour of \nKendriya Vidyalaya Sangathan and also provide the necessary tem porary \naccommodation for runn ing the vidyalaya before administrative o rders for \nopening of this KV are issued.    \n(e)  A KV at Devgarh is already f unctioning in the District of Rajsamand. A \nproposal in the prescribed profo rmahas been received by Kendriy a Vidyalaya \nSangathan(KVS) from the Government of Rajasthan, for opening of  a new KV \nat Bhim, District, Rajsamand, in which neither the proposed lan d nor the \ntemporary building has been found suitable as per norms of KVS.   \n \n***** \n \n\nANNEXURE \n \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (d) OF THE LOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 14 FOR 18\nth NOVEMBER, 2019 RAISED BY MS. DIYA \nKUMARI, HON’BLE MEMBERS OF PARLIAMENT REGARDING NEW KENDRIYA \nVIDYALAYAS \n \n \nDetails of 76 Kendriya Vidyalayas functioning in the State of Rajasthan \n(As on 13.11.2019) \n \n S.No. Name of Kendriya Vidyalaya Sector Year of opening \n1 AJMER NO.I (CRPF) CIVIL 1985-86 \n2 AJMER NO.II (CRPF) CIVIL 1986-87 \n3 ALWAR CIVIL 1965-66 \n4 ANOOPGARH (BSF) CIVIL 1986-87 \n5 BANSWARA CIVIL 1987-88 \n6 BARAN CIVIL 1996-97 \n7 BEAWAR, AJMER CIVIL 1993-94 \n8 BHARATPUR CIVIL 1973-74 \n9 BHILWARA CIVIL 1994-95 \n10 CHURU CIVIL 1989-90 \n11 DABLA (BSF) CIVIL 1996-97 \n12 DEOLI (CISF) CIVIL 1984-85 \n13 GANGAPUR CITY CIVIL 2003-04 \n14 JAIPUR NO.I (BAJAJ NAGAR) CIVIL 1964-65 \n15 JAIPUR NO.III (MREC) CIVIL 1982-83 \n16 JAIPUR NO.V (MANSAROVER) CIVIL 1994-95 \n17 JAIPUR NO.VI (PRATAP NAGA R) (SECTOR III) CIVIL 1997-98 \n18 JHALAWAR CIVIL 1995-96 \n19 JHUNJHUNU CIVIL 1986-87 \n20 JODHPUR (BSF) CIVIL 1971-72 \n21 KARAULI CIVIL 2004-05 \n22 KOTA NO.II CIVIL 1994-95 \n23 MOUNTABU (CRPF